\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(2,- 3 \\pi)}(x-(2)) \\\\ z-(5) & =(- 3 \\pi - 1)(x-(2)) \\\\ z & =- 3 \\pi x - x + 7 + 6 \\pi\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(2,- 3 \\pi,5)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=- 3 \\pi \\\\ z &=- 3 \\pi x - x + 7 + 6 \\pi\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186518892 :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2 \\\\ z &=- 8 y - 33\\end{aligned}\\right."] [17592186518893 :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=-4 \\\\ z &=8 x - 17\\end{aligned}\\right."]}
